	'k17ccb915' => 'To allow our radiologists to tailor imaging protocols accurately, referrals should include the patient\'s full demographic details, contact telephone number, relevant medical history, specific clinical question, and the requested anatomical region. If the patient has undergone previous imaging at another institution, noting this on the request enables us to arrange image transfer for direct longitudinal comparison. For CT referrals involving intravenous contrast, please provide recent renal function markers where available. Clear clinical questions allow our radiographers and radiologists to focus precisely on the underlying pathology.',
