	'k6087b79c' => 'Diagnostic imaging is only as valuable as the clarity and timeliness of the written report. At Nagi Imaging, our entire workflow is engineered around a four-stage process that delivers definitive interpretations the same working day.',
	'k60e676c9' => 'Read referrer notes',
	'k60e9253d' => 'CT, MRI, ultrasound, X-ray, DEXA and mammography accepted — scans before 15:00 reported by 18:00',
	'k6288a86e' => 'What the clinic did next',
	'k62a16b9b' => 'Our clinical team brings dedicated diagnostic expertise to Grand Canal Dock: three consultant radiologists, a lead radiographer, a sonographer, a radiographer and the coordinator who keeps every referral moving.',
	'k62b9a7b7' => 'Complex cross-sectional imaging carries nuances that benefit substantially from peer review. Dr. Amira Haddad, Dr. Lukas Brenner, and Dr. Siobhán Kerr share the reporting workload so that every CT and MRI dataset is read twice. The first radiologist documents primary findings, anatomical measurements, and clinical impressions. The second radiologist independently opens the raw image slices, reviews the prior clinical history, and verifies all observations. This collaborative discipline reduces diagnostic discrepancies, clarifies borderline presentations, and provides referring clinicians with total confidence in the reported radiological findings.',
	'k62da60e1' => 'Modality expansion: introducing MRI in 2019',
