	'k71958e03' => 'CT and MRI',
	'k733555e7' => 'The report can take a week.',
	'k74817cd5' => 'Every study follows an unhurried, four-stage protocol: referral, scan, read, and report. Following receipt of the electronic or phone referral, the patient is scanned by an experienced radiographer over a fifteen to forty-five minute appointment. Within two hours of scan completion, the primary consultant radiologist undertakes the first interpretation. For CT and MRI examinations, a second consultant independently reviews the entire image series before findings are finalized. For all scans completed before 15:00, the signed diagnostic report is securely delivered to the referring physician by 18:00 the same working day, with patient copies provided upon clinician authorization.',
	'k748e3558' => 'Step-free entrance from the quay; paid parking at Calder Quay car park. A four-minute walk from the tram stop. Referral phone line Mon–Fri 08:00–17:00; Sunday closed.',
