	'kb331b918' => 'By 18:00',
	'kb348d1af' => 'What information is required on the referral request?',
	'kb34e9fe9' => 'Nagi Imaging is situated at 14 Calder Quay, Grand Canal Dock, Dublin 2. Our premises feature level, step-free access directly from the quay, offering full accessibility for wheelchairs, mobility scooters, and walking aids. If using public transport, the Grand Canal Dock tram stop is a level four-minute walk from our entrance. For those travelling by private vehicle, paid visitor parking is available at the Calder Quay car park adjacent to the building. Our reception team is on hand throughout the day to assist patients requiring arrival support or accompaniment into our scanning rooms.',
	'kb42a9b2d' => 'Scans from your clinic,',
	'kb6883e88' => 'Report: by 18:00 the same working day for scans before 15:00. Read by two radiologists.',
	'kb6c7117a' => 'Grace Achterberg',
	'kb710d57a' => 'That week is the hardest part.',
	'kb7bb815a' => 'Nagi Imaging provides six focused diagnostic modalities for patients referred by clinics across Dublin. Every study is scheduled with dedicated preparation guidance and reported promptly according to our same-day standard.',
	'kb89b65d7' => 'First read within two hours; CT and MRI read twice.',
	'kb8c90bac' => 'Nagi Imaging opened its doors in 2016 at 14 Calder Quay, Grand Canal Dock, Dublin 2. Founders Dr. Amira Haddad and Tomás Oyelaran recognized a persistent frustration among local general practitioners: while modern imaging scans take only minutes to acquire, patients and doctors often waited up to a week for a written report. Operating from a quiet outpatient suite overlooking the water, Nagi Imaging began with a single high-specification CT scanner and an uncompromising founding rule: patients scanned in the morning would have their finalized radiological reports delivered before clinics closed that same evening.',
	'kb90f60d3' => 'We also had one question.',
	'kba3351de' => 'Patient preparation varies strictly by modality to ensure diagnostic accuracy. Patients scheduled for CT with contrast must fast from solid food for four hours prior to arrival, while staying well hydrated with clear water. Pelvic ultrasound scans require a full bladder, achieved by drinking one litre of water one hour beforehand. Mammography patients should avoid applying deodorant, talcum powder, or lotions to the chest or underarms on the day of the examination. DEXA patients must omit calcium supplements for 24 hours prior to scanning. Patients attending for MRI must complete our standard safety checklist regarding metallic implants before entering the scanner room.',
	'kbbaff128' => 'Contact',
	'kbbf8e15f' => 'Card or bank transfer,',
	'kbc6d58ce' => 'Mon–Fri 08:00–17:00',
	'kbcc254b5' => 'Phone',
	'kbe9f3e4c' => 'Dr. Amira Haddad is our medical director, consultant radiologist, and co-founder. With subspecialty expertise in body CT and MRI interpretation, Dr. Haddad established our double-reading protocols and oversees diagnostic standards across the practice. She works in daily partnership with co-founder and lead radiographer Tomás Oyelaran. Tomás brings extensive clinical leadership in advanced CT and MRI scanning protocols, patient positioning, and radiation protection. Together, they established Nagi Imaging in 2016 at Calder Quay, proving that an independent outpatient imaging room can consistently deliver comprehensive diagnostic reports on the day of scanning.',
	'kbeb4e437' => 'Our imaging centre is open Monday to Friday from 07:30 to 19:00, and Saturdays from 08:00 to 13:00; we are closed on Sundays. Referring clinicians and medical secretaries can reach our dedicated referral line on +353 1 555 0148, operating Monday to Friday from 08:00 to 17:00 and managed by Grace Achterberg. Written referral documents and clinical requests should be directed to referrals@nagi-imaging.example. For general patient inquiries, appointment scheduling, and receipt requests, please contact our administrative team at hello@nagi-imaging.example.',
	'kbef66064' => 'we take it from there.',
