	'keface63c' => 'Could a report be ready',
	'kf2542a85' => 'For referring doctors',
	'kf35ecce3' => 'Different examinations require specific preparation to ensure clear imagery. For a CT scan requiring intravenous contrast, do not consume food for four hours prior to your appointment, though drinking clear water is encouraged. If you are booked for an MRI, wear comfortable clothing free from metal zips, hooks, or metallic threads, and notify staff of any internal implants or pacemaker devices. Pelvic ultrasound requires a comfortably full bladder; please finish drinking one litre of water one hour before your scan. For mammography, avoid using antiperspirant, perfume, or body powder. DEXA patients must avoid calcium supplements for 24 hours prior to their scan.',
